welcome back a huge turnout today for  the annual  walk with the heart of a child event its  goal is to raise funds to support  children who are born with congenital  heart disease  eight news now reporter victoria saha  was there she has our story  the 18th annual walk with the heart of a  child event  is meant to honor those we've lost too  young and for those who are still  fighting congenital heart disease  today's event brought out hundreds of  people  making up for last year's event that was  canceled  the one mile walk may have seemed short  but the turnout goes a long way  for the children's heart foundation more  than 67 teams signed up to walk in this  year's event  with 8 news now meteorologist sheri  swank the emcee  families and kids participated to raise  funds to support the children who were  born with heart defects  studies show one in 100 children are  born with  congenital heart disease each year in  the united states  and many don't survive the first time  right after birth  i was able to take her home for a good  two months and then we went back for her  second surgery  she lasted another month and a half in  the hospital and then i just wasn't able  to bring her home with me  garcia's daughter died at six months  with seven different heart defects  garcia participates in the walk in honor  of her daughter elea  many of the families i spoke with today  say they each have their own battle with  this disease  but participating in this walk makes  them feel like they're not alone  in this fight reporting from craig ranch  regional park victoria zaha
 

